WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.540
Citizens of Gotham, Batman is once again coming
to bust some bad guys.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:09.040
And it sounds like the latest iteration of
the Caped Crusader will be more conflicted

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:09.580
than ever.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.740
At least that's the word from the actor who's
set to don the cape and cowl in the upcoming

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.080
superhero flick The Batman.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.340
Robert Pattinson recently sat down with The
New York Times' Kyle Buchanan, who took the

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.500
opportunity to ask Pattinson about his role
as the Dark Knight in the soon-to-shoot Batman

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.280
movie.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.160
The actor was quick to praise director Matt
Reeves, and offered his own read of the notoriously

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.480
complex superhero he's about to play.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.040
He gushed:

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.400
"I love the director, Matt Reeves, and it's
a dope character.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.240
His morality is a little bit off.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.250
He's not the golden boy, unlike almost every
other comic-book character.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.500
There is a simplicity to his worldview, but
where it sits is strange, which allows you

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.060
to have more scope with the character."

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:52.640
The actor then revealed why he was drawn to
the character - and in doing so, he made a

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.500
head-turning comment about Batman.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:55.540
Pattinson said:

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.510
"Batman's not a hero.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.680
He's a complicated character.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.960
I don't think I could ever play a real hero
- there's always got to be something a little

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:03.600
bit wrong."

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.180
By the sounds of it, Pattinson and Reeves
are apparently aiming to take the "hero" out

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.200
of the superhero genre with The Batman - which
is some of the most intriguing news we've

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.720
heard about the new movie thus far.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.720
And that's saying a lot in a week that's also
seen The Batman cast Zoë Kravitz as Selina

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.600
Kyle - a.k.a. Catwoman - and set its sights
on Paul Dano as the Riddler.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.800
All of that came just weeks after it was reported
that Westworld star Jeffrey Wright was in

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.120
talks to appear as Batman's Gotham City Police
Department ally Commissioner Gordon.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.659
Though we've got to admit that it's initially
shocking to hear Pattinson say that Batman

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:41.610
isn't a hero, it's not exactly an earth-shattering
revelation to learn that the actor and director

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.640
Matt Reeves plan to subvert the norm.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.200
That vision was first teased with the news
that Reeves' was scrapping Ben Affleck's script

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.710
for The Batman, and furthered when Affleck
himself was relieved of his dark watch over

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.540
the streets of Gotham.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.300
"NOOOO!"

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.860
In spite of its initial production turmoil,
The Batman soldiered on with Reeves at the

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.860
helm - though months passed with little to
no news of what the director had in mind.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.340
The silence finally broke earlier this year
when Reeves revealed that his movie would

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.840
be a, quote, "point of view-driven, noir Batman
tale" that sees Batman flexing his detective

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.040
skills that most films have barely touched
on.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.670
At the time, Reeves told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.230
"I hope it's going to be a story that will
be thrilling but also emotional.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.120
It's more Batman in his detective mode than
we've seen in the films [...] It's going to

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.700
allow his character to have an arc so that
he can go through a transformation."

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.680
When it was announced that Pattinson had been
tapped to don the mask in The Batman, the

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.310
internet nearly imploded at the news, with
the actor himself even fearing the wrath of

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.640
an insolent internet fandom.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.800
While most of those fans were intrigued by
the thought of Pattinson in the Bat-suit,

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.680
there were plenty who were wary of the former
Twilight heartthrob bringing the requisite

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.060
charm and menace required with the dual roles
of Bruce Wayne and Batman.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.210
But fans have little to worry about.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:58.770
Pattinson has spent his post-Twilight years
forging a reputation as one of the most fiercely

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:04.330
devoted and adventurous actors on the planet
- a reputation he's earned by delivering show-stopping

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.300
performances in indie fare like Cosmopolis,
Good Time, High Life, and the just-released

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.640
film The Lighthouse.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:16.060
Though The Batman will serve as the highest-profile
film Pattinson has appeared in in years, there's

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.920
little doubt the actor will bring the same
sort of intensity to his role as the Dark

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.420
Knight.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.220
Sadly, it'll be awhile before we see what
comes from his enticing approach to the role.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:31.540
The Batman will begin filming in early 2020,
but won't be out in theaters until June 25th,

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.100
2021.

